    "text": "We r\u00e6da\u00f0 on \u00feisum Drihtenlican symbeld\u00e6ge \u00fe\u00e6t halige godspell be \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes acennednysse,\nBe him god geswutelode on \u00fe\u00e6re gastlican gesih\u00f0e, \u00e6rest \u00feurh Ezechiel & eft on Apocalypsi, on earnes\n\u00d0a \u00fery o\u00f0re godspelleras awriton heora godspell be Cristes menniscnysse, hu he to mannum com, &\n\u00d0a b\u00e6don \u00fea bisceopas binnan Asian lande \u00feone halgan Iohannem \u00fe\u00e6t he him awrite sume gewissunge\nAnd he him bead \u00fea \u00fereora daga f\u00e6sten, & \u00e6fter \u00feam f\u00e6stene he wear\u00f0 swa afylled mid \u00feam Halgan\n\u00d0is w\u00e6s on anginne mid \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan Gode.\nEalle \u00feing syndon gesceapene \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6t Word, & butan \u00feam Worde nis geworht nan \u00feing.\n\u00d0\u00e6t geworht is w\u00e6s lif on him sylfum, & \u00fe\u00e6t lif witodlice w\u00e6s manna leoht.\nAnd \u00fe\u00e6t leoht scean on \u00f0eostrum, & \u00fea \u00f0eostru ne underfengon \u00fe\u00e6t fores\u00e6de leoht.\nSum man w\u00e6s asend fram Gode sylfum to us, & his nama w\u00e6s witodlice Iohannes.\n\u00d0es com on gecy\u00f0nysse \u00fe\u00e6t he cydde be \u00f0am leohte so\u00f0e gecy\u00f0nysse, \u00fe\u00e6t ealle gelyfdon \u00feurh hine.\nN\u00e6s he na him sylf leoht, ac \u00fe\u00e6t he cydde gecy\u00f0nesse be \u00feam leohte.\n\u00d0\u00e6t so\u00f0e leoht w\u00e6s \u00fee onliht \u00e6lcne mannan \u00fee on \u00feisne middaneard becym\u00f0 to menn geboren.\nOn middanearde he w\u00e6s, & \u00fees middaneard w\u00e6s geworht eall \u00feurh hine, & middaneard ne oncneow\nOn his agenum he com, & his agene ne underfengon hine.\nSwa fela swa hine underfengon, \u00feam he forgeaf anweald Godes bearn to beonne, \u00feam \u00fee on his naman\nAnd \u00fe\u00e6t Word is geworht fl\u00e6sc & hit wunode on us.\nAnd we sylfe gesawon so\u00f0lice his wuldor, swylc wuldor swa gedafena\u00f0 Godes ancennedan Suna, eall\nAugustinus se wisa & se wordsnotera bisceop s\u00e6de \u00fe\u00e6t he ne mihte gehyran \u00feonne he him sylf w\u00e6s\nAc he asmeade \u00feeah hw\u00e6\u00f0re sume \u00fea getacnunge \u00feurh Godes sylfes fultum \u00fe\u00e6s & be his onwrigenysse\nSe so\u00f0f\u00e6sta godspellere us s\u00e6de \u00feurh God \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t Word w\u00e6s on anginne mid \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan Gode:\nBe \u00feam awrat Moyses se m\u00e6ra heretoga, In principio fecit Deus celum et terram: God geworhte on\nWe cwe\u00f0a\u00f0 eft gyt be \u00feam ylcan anginne \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t Word w\u00e6s on anginne mid \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan Gode.\n& se sealmwyrhta sang be \u00feam Worde swa swa we her secga\u00f0 eow to swutelunge: Uerbo Domini c\u00e6li\nHer is nu belocen on \u00feysum lytlan ferse eall seo halige \u00f0rynnys \u00fee is \u00ferymwealdend God: se f\u00e6der &\n\u00d0a halgan englas \u00fee on heofonum wunia\u00f0 syndon gesta\u00feelf\u00e6ste & gestrangode swi\u00f0e \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6t halige\nEft sang se sealmwyrhta on sumum o\u00f0rum sealme: Quam magnificata sunt opera tua, Domine: omnia in\n\u00c6r he sang be \u00feam Worde, & \u00e6fter be \u00feam Wisdome.\nPaulus se apostol eac on his pistole awrat be urum H\u00e6lende criste & cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he w\u00e6re \u00fe\u00e6s halgan\nEac s\u00e6don sume h\u00e6\u00f0ne on heora gesetnessum \u00fe\u00e6t we sceolon gelyfan on \u00feone so\u00fean god \u00fee wilt \u00fea\nAn h\u00e6\u00f0en mann w\u00e6s iu on egypta lande \u00e6r cristes acennednysse, & he cydde be Criste, Hermes\nHe awrat ane boc, \u00fee hatte \u00feuss on Leden: Uerbum Perfectum, \u00fe\u00e6t is, Fulfremed Word.\nWord \u00fe\u00e6t ge magon gehyran hu se so\u00f0lice oncneow: Filius benedicti Dei atque bon\u00e6 uoluntatis, cuius\n\u00d0us wrat se Hermes on his gesetnysse be \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan F\u00e6der & his ancennedan Suna, & het hine\nFela we mihton secgan swylcera gewitnyssa \u00feurh h\u00e6\u00f0ene witegan be \u00feam heofonlican Gode, gyf us to\nOn anginne w\u00e6s Word, & \u00fe\u00e6t Word w\u00e6s mid Gode, and \u00fe\u00e6t Word w\u00e6s God.\n\u00d0is w\u00e6s on anginne mid \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan Gode.\nSume gedwolmen dweledon on geleafan & noldon gelyfan \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6s lyfigendan Godes Sunu w\u00e6re \u00e6fre\nHer ge magon gehyran on \u00feisum halgan godspelle \u00fe\u00e6t o\u00f0er is se F\u00e6der, o\u00f0er is se Sunu, & o\u00f0er is se\nSeo an godcundnyss \u00fee him eallum is gem\u00e6ne nele na ge\u00feafian \u00fe\u00e6t hi \u00fery godas syndon, ne \u00fe\u00e6t heora\nEalle \u00feing syndon gesceapene \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6t Word, & butan \u00feam Worde nis geworht nan \u00feing.\nNis he na gesceapen, ne he nis na gesceaft, \u00feurh \u00feone \u00f0e syndon ealle \u00feing gesceapene.\nEalle \u00fea gesceafta gesewenlice on worulde & \u00fea ungesewenlican on \u00feam uppheofone \u00fee \u00e6nige\n\u00d0a gesceafta syndon gesette on \u00ferim \u00feingum, In mensura et numero et pondere; \u00fe\u00e6t is on Engliscere\nN\u00e6s n\u00e6fre nan synn \u00feurh god gesceapen ne nan unrihtwisnyss ne yfel \u00feurh hine ac \u00feurh Godes willan\n& eft \u00feurh Adam on his forg\u00e6gednysse.\nN\u00e6f\u00f0 yfel nane wununge \u00fe\u00e6t hit wesan m\u00e6ge ahw\u00e6r buton on gesceaftum \u00fee gode w\u00e6ron\nGode w\u00e6ron \u00fea englas fram Gode gesceapene & \u00fe\u00e6t yfel n\u00e6s \u00fea gyt nahw\u00e6r wunigende, ac hi hit\nGod gesceop heofonas, him sylfum to wununge & his halgum englum \u00fee him gehyrsumedon, & eac\nAc \u00e6fter Adames gylte us w\u00e6s seo eor\u00f0e bet\u00e6ht on to wunigenne on \u00feissere worulde, & God us \u00feeah\nNytenu & orfcynn he forgeaf us to fultume, & wyrta to l\u00e6cedome & to wlite \u00fe\u00e6re eor\u00fean, & orfe to\nManega gesceafta mislice us drecca\u00f0 eall for urum synnum, \u00fe\u00e6t we swa tocnawon hw\u00e6s we wyr\u00f0e\n\u00d0in gelica \u00fee cwy\u00f0 to sum teonfullic word; \u00f0u modegast ongean, & ne miht \u00f0e bewerian wi\u00f0 flean on\nSwa w\u00e6s iu Pharao, \u00fee wann ongean God, se Egiptisca cyning, swa swa us cydde Moyses, \u00fe\u00e6t God\nEa\u00f0e mihte God, gyf he swa wolde, sendan beran & leon ongean \u00feam breman cyninge, dracan eac &\nOft man wyrc\u00f0 nu isen of eor\u00f0an gold & seolfor ac hi ne mihte nan mann macian to wecgum gyf God\nNe fur\u00f0on \u00e6nne sticcan ne \u00e6nne st\u00e6f we n\u00e6fdon ne ane ofl\u00e6tan to urum m\u00e6ssan gode gyf he us ne\n\u00d0a deoplican drymen mid heora drycr\u00e6ftum on Egypta lande \u00fee forl\u00e6rdon Farao worhton manega\nGe ne magon na swi\u00f0or, \u00feeah \u00f0e we eow secgon, heora scincr\u00e6ft tocnawan, ac us secga\u00f0 lareowas\nWe secga\u00f0 nu for\u00f0 on embe \u00feis so\u00f0e godspell: \u00f0\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t geworht is w\u00e6s lif on him sylfum.\n\u00d0eos eor\u00f0e is geworht, ac heo nis na hyre sylf lif, ac on \u00feam wisdome \u00fee geworhte \u00fea eor\u00fean is \u00fe\u00e6t\n\u00d0u sceawast \u00fea heofonan & sunnan & monan; hi synd on \u00feam cr\u00e6fte, we cwe\u00f0a\u00f0 nu swutelicor, on\nAnd \u00fe\u00e6t lif witodlice w\u00e6s manna leoht.\n\u00d0\u00e6ra manna leoht he is \u00fee gelyfa\u00f0 on hine, swa swa he sylf cw\u00e6\u00f0 on sumon godspelle: Ego sum lux\nAnd \u00fe\u00e6t leoht scean on \u00feystrum, & \u00fea \u00f0eostru ne underfengon \u00fe\u00e6t fores\u00e6de leoht.\nSwa swa \u00fe\u00e6re sunnan leoht bescin\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6ne blindan, & se blinda ne gesih\u00f0 \u00feone scinendan leoman, swa\nSum mann w\u00e6s asend fram Gode sylfum to us, & his nama w\u00e6s witodlice Iohannes.\nHe w\u00e6s fram Gode asend \u00fe\u00e6t he secgan mihte so\u00f0e gecy\u00f0nysse, swa swa her \u00e6fter seg\u00f0 on \u00feisum\nSwa swa se d\u00e6gsteorra on d\u00e6gered up g\u00e6\u00f0 \u00e6tforan \u00fe\u00e6re sunnan, swa scean Iohannes \u00e6tforan cristes\nN\u00e6s he na him sylf leoht, ac \u00fe\u00e6t he cydde gecy\u00f0nysse be \u00feam leohte.\nSe h\u00e6lend s\u00e6de be him on sumere stowe \u00fe\u00e6t he leohtf\u00e6t w\u00e6re beorhte lixende for \u00fean \u00fee he bodode\nSe H\u00e6lend s\u00e6de eac to his halgum apostolum, Vos estis lux mundi: Ge syndon middaneardes leoht,\nPaulus cw\u00e6\u00f0 eac to \u00feam geleaffullum: Hwilon ge w\u00e6ron \u00feeostru, nu ge syndon leoht on Gode; for\n\u00c6c ure eagan syndon gehatene leoht, ac hi naht ne geseo\u00f0 butan hi sum leoht habbon, o\u00f0\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6s d\u00e6ges\nNu seg\u00f0 se godspellere be \u00feam so\u00f0an leohte, \u00f0\u00e6t so\u00f0e leoht w\u00e6s \u00fee onliht \u00e6lcne mannan \u00fee on \u00feisne\n\u00d0\u00e6t so\u00f0e leoht is ure leofa H\u00e6lend, \u00fee is him sylf leoht & onliht \u00e6lcne mann \u00fee his geleafan leoht on\nOn middanearde he w\u00e6s, & \u00fees middaneard w\u00e6s eall geworht \u00feurh hine, & middaneard ne oncneow\nHe w\u00e6s on middanearde \u00feurh his godcundnysse, & he com to middanearde \u00feurh his menniscnysse, &\n\u00d0\u00e6t syndon \u00fea ungeleaffullan men \u00f0e his geleafan forsawon.\n\u00d0is is swa ges\u00e6d be sumum mannum her, ac manega gelyfdon of \u00feisum middanearde, ge of\nSwa fela swa hine underfengon, eallum hiom he forgeaf anweald Godes bearn to beonne, \u00feam \u00fee on\nHer ge magon gehyran \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes cystignysse & his micclan godnysse ofer manna bearnum \u00fe\u00e6t\nMicel m\u00e6r\u00f0 is \u00feis, & miccle ge\u00feing\u00f0u, \u00fe\u00e6t se \u00e6lmihtiga God \u00feurh his godnysse het us menn godas, &\nBe \u00feam ylcan cw\u00e6\u00f0 iu God sylf to Moysen: Ecce constitui te deum Pharaonis; et Aaron frater tuus erit\nSwa micelne Moyse \u00fe\u00e6t he hine gesette swylcum cyninge to gode, \u00fee ann wi\u00f0 God sylfne, ac him\nBe \u00feisum sang eac se sealmwyrhta \u00feus: Deus stetit in synagoga deorum: in medio autem deos\nCrist is ancenned Sunu of \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan F\u00e6der; nu nolde he ana beon butan he gebro\u00f0ra h\u00e6fde,\n\u00d0a \u00fee na of blodum ne of \u00fe\u00e6s fl\u00e6sces willan ne of weres willan, ac \u00f0a \u00fee of Gode synd acennede.\nNe bi\u00f0 na of \u00feam blode \u00fees halga bearnteam, ne of weres gestreone, ne of wifes cenninge, ac of Godes\n\u00d0\u00e6t \u00fee of fl\u00e6sce bi\u00f0 acenned, \u00fe\u00e6t bi\u00f0 fl\u00e6sc witodlice, & \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fee bi\u00f0 acenned of gaste, \u00fe\u00e6t bi\u00f0 eac\nAnd \u00fe\u00e6t Word is geworht fl\u00e6sc, & hit wunode on us.\nNis \u00fe\u00e6t halige Word awend to fl\u00e6sce, ac se heofonlica \u00e6\u00feeling her on \u00feas woruld com & \u00fea\nNu cw\u00e6don \u00fea Mannichei, \u00fea manfullan gedwolan, \u00fe\u00e6t Gode w\u00e6re unwur\u00f0 on his m\u00e6gen\u00ferymnysse\nAc gehyre se dysega & se gedwola secgan \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t halige m\u00e6den, \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes modor, n\u00e6fde nane\nGyf seo sunne scin\u00f0, swa swa we geseo\u00f0 oft, on fulum adelan & heo befyled ne bi\u00f0, micele swi\u00f0or\nAnd we sylfe gesawon so\u00f0lice his wuldor, swylc wuldor swa gedafena\u00f0 Godes ancennedan Suna.\n\u00d0a apostoli gesawon \u00fee si\u00f0edon mid him \u00fea wundra \u00fee he worhte, & hu he wear\u00f0 hwilon uppan anre\nEft hi hine gesawon sy\u00f0\u00f0an he of dea\u00f0e aras on ansundum lichaman, & hu he astah to heofonum, &\nIohannes se fulluhtere hine gefullode on \u00fe\u00e6re ea iordanen, & Crist \u00fea up eode ut of \u00feam w\u00e6tere &\nEft sy\u00f0\u00f0an on \u00feam munte, \u00fea \u00fee him mid w\u00e6ron \u00fea \u00fea he swa beorhte scean, swa swa we s\u00e6don \u00e6r,\n\u00d0us s\u00e6de Matheus.\nEft on \u00feriddan si\u00f0e, \u00e6r Cristes \u00ferowunge, clypode se ylca F\u00e6der cu\u00f0lice him to, \u00fe\u00e6t eall \u00fe\u00e6t folc\nNu w\u00e6s \u00feis micel wuldor & micel gewitnyss \u00feam Suna, \u00fe\u00e6t se F\u00e6der swa \u00feriwa \u00feuss clypode him to\n\u00d0\u00e6t godspell geenda\u00f0 nu on \u00feisum wordum \u00feuss: Eall fulne mid gyfe & mid so\u00f0f\u00e6stnysse.\nOn \u00fe\u00e6re menniscnysse he h\u00e6fde swa micele gyfe \u00fe\u00e6t he w\u00e6s so\u00f0 God & so\u00f0 mann geboren, Dauides\nSo\u00f0f\u00e6stnysse he h\u00e6f\u00f0, swa he sylf s\u00e6de: Ego sum uia, & ueritas, & uita: Ic sylf eom se weg, &\n\u00d0urh Moysen w\u00e6s gesett \u00feam ealdum mannum iu \u00e6, & open lagu, & se leofa H\u00e6lend gebrohte us\n\u00d0am is wuldor & lof & wyr\u00f0mynt on ecnysse mid \u00feam heofonlican F\u00e6der & \u00feam Halgan Gaste on",
